<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:x="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:excel" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><x:ExcelWorkbook><x:ExcelWorksheets><x:ExcelWorksheet><x:Name>Worksheet</x:Name><x:WorksheetOptions><x:DisplayGridlines/></x:WorksheetOptions></x:ExcelWorksheet></x:ExcelWorksheets></x:ExcelWorkbook></xml><![endif]--></head><body><table>
    
    
   
   <thead>      
      <tr>
         <th aria-label=" Game Number Which game out of all played by this team." data-stat="team_game" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center" data-tip="<strong>Game Number</strong><br>Which game out of all played by this team.">Gm#</th>
         <th aria-label="A number in parentheses indicates which game of a doubleheader. Click dates for box scores of games or standings on this day." data-stat="date_game" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center" data-tip="A number in parentheses indicates which game of a doubleheader.<br>Click dates for box scores of games or standings on this day.">Date</th>
         <th aria-label="boxscore" data-stat="boxscore" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center"></th>
         <th aria-label="Tm" data-stat="team_ID" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting center">Tm</th>
         <th aria-label=" Home or Away Game @ means it is an away game, blank means home." data-stat="homeORvis" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting left" data-tip="<strong>Home or Away Game</strong><br>@ means it is an away game, blank means home.">&nbsp;</th>
         <th aria-label="Opp" data-stat="opp_ID" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting center">Opp</th>
         <th aria-label=" Win/Loss/Tie -wo indicates it was a walkoff win or loss. May miss some of those pre-1973, and none before 1940." data-stat="win_loss_result" scope="col" class=" poptip show_partial_when_sorting center" data-tip="<strong>Win/Loss/Tie</strong><br>-wo indicates it was a walkoff win or loss. May miss some of those pre-1973, and none before 1940.">W/L</th>
         <th aria-label="Runs Scored" data-stat="R" scope="col" class=" poptip center" data-tip="Runs Scored/Allowed">R</th>
         <th aria-label="Runs Allowed" data-stat="RA" scope="col" class=" poptip center" data-tip="Runs Allowed">RA</th>
         <th aria-label=" Innings Only shown if something other than 9 innings were played." data-stat="extra_innings" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting center" data-tip="<strong>Innings</strong><br>Only shown if something other than 9 innings were played.">Inn</th>
         <th aria-label=" Win Loss Record Team&amp;#x2019;s overall record after this game." data-stat="win_loss_record" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting center" data-tip="<strong>Win Loss Record</strong><br>Team&amp;#x2019;s overall record after this game.">W-L</th>
         <th aria-label="Rank" data-stat="rank" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting center">Rank</th>
         <th aria-label="Games Back" data-stat="games_back" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center" data-tip="<strong>Games Back of Division/League Leader</strong><br>Computed as games over .500 of leader (W-L) minus games over .500 of team divided by two.<br>Typically computed at the end of play for a particular day.<br>Blank for 1st game of DH.">GB</th>
         <th aria-label="Win" data-stat="winning_pitcher" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center">Win</th>
         <th aria-label="Loss" data-stat="losing_pitcher" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center">Loss</th>
         <th aria-label="Save" data-stat="saving_pitcher" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center">Save</th>
         <th aria-label=" Time of Game " data-stat="time_of_game" scope="col" class=" poptip center" data-tip="<strong>Time of Game</strong>">Time</th>
         <th aria-label="Day or Night Game Determined by the start time of the game as stated by RetroSheet. We rely on their designation here." data-stat="day_or_night" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center" data-tip="Day or Night Game<br>Determined by the start time of the game as stated by RetroSheet.<br>We rely on their designation here.">D/N</th>
         <th aria-label=" Attendance Typically, tickets sold in home games." data-stat="attendance" scope="col" class=" poptip center" data-tip="<strong>Attendance</strong><br>Typically, tickets sold in home games.">Attendance</th>
         <th aria-label=" Championship Leverage Index The importance of this game on the team's probability of winning the World Series. 1.0 is average importance, below 1.0 is below average importance and above 1.0 is above average importance." data-stat="cli" scope="col" class=" poptip hide_non_quals center" data-tip="<strong>Championship Leverage Index</strong><br>The importance of this game on the team's probability of winning the World Series.<br>1.0 is average importance, below 1.0 is below average importance and above 1.0 is above average importance." data-filter="1" data-name="<strong>Championship Leverage Index</strong><br>The importance of this game on the team's probability of winning the World Series.<br>1.0 is average importance, below 1.0 is below average importance and above 1.0 is above average importance.">cLI</th>
         <th aria-label=" Win Loss Streak + means a winning streak, - means a losing streak." data-stat="win_loss_streak" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc show_partial_when_sorting center" data-tip="<strong>Win Loss Streak</strong><br>+ means a winning streak, - means a losing streak.">Streak</th>
         <th aria-label="Originally Scheduled Game DateIf this is a makeup game, the original game date. The reason for the reschedule is in parentheses." data-stat="reschedule" scope="col" class=" poptip sort_default_asc center" data-tip="<strong>Originally Scheduled Game Date</strong><br>If this is a makeup game, the original game date. The reason for the reschedule is in parentheses.">Orig. Scheduled</th>
      </tr>
      </thead>
